<title>JAPAN: IBM launches 5.0 pct yen/dlr samurais-Daiwa.</title>
<headline>IBM launches 5.0 pct yen/dlr samurais-Daiwa.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Daiwa Securities on Friday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  International Business Machines Corp (IBM)</p>
<p> AMT		 50 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    5.0 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  22 Aug 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  24 Feb 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Feb 4 to Feb 21</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P A, Moody's A1</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Daiwa Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>NOTES: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $4,105.10 for each 500,000 yen bond held at maturity. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
